WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W21 (0.3.1)


STATE

  Version 0.3.1, Phase P4 in progress ([[ ]], local/declare, brace
  expansion), on branch dev. 0.3.1 adds:
  - linear-time POSIX ERE engine (Thompson NFA / PikeVM, submatch
    captures, bounded compile/exec, immune to ReDoS) in
    include/tam-clam/regex.h and src/regex.c (no PCRE or libc regcomp);
  - [[ ... ]] conditional compound command in include/tam-clam/cond.h,
    src/cond.c, src/parse.c, src/lex.c, src/func.c, src/lint.c,
    src/exec.c, and src/edit/highlight.c: &&, ||, !, (), == / != glob
    patterns, =~ with BASH_REMATCH, < / >, arithmetic -eq..-ge, -v, -o,
    and file/string tests;
  - dynamic function-local variable scopes (local, declare local by
    default inside functions, declare -g) and full declare attributes
    (-i integer arithmetic/+=, -l lowercase, -u uppercase, -F function
    names) in src/var.c, src/bi_declare.c, src/exec.c, and src/builtins.c;
  - brace expansion ({a,b}, nested braces, Cartesian products, and
    {start..end[..incr]} integer/char/zero-padded sequences with depth
    and word-count limits) in include/tam-clam/brace.h, src/brace.c,
    and src/expand.c;
  - tests/test_regex.c (48 checks), tests/test_brace.c (42 checks),
    tests/test_cond.c (24 checks), tests/spec/cond.test.sh (10 cases),
    tests/spec/local-declare.test.sh (9 cases), tests/spec/brace.test.sh
    (7 cases, all verified against bash --posix), fuzz seeds, and
    sandbox/demo-0.3.1-cond-local-brace.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test, make sanitize, and make
  fuzz pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


